step	38	-	Quick guide step 38
line	<str>Go to the Exam Centre south of the Digsite. (Varrock teleport then run east; or use a Digsite pendant/ teleport and walk south towards the exam centre; the Senntisten teleport from the Ancient Spellbook is quite close, and can be used from a Portal Nexus in a POH)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the most north-eastern of the south-eastern bookcases to find a beaten book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the beaten book, then read the scroll.</str>
line	
line	<str>Keep the book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head back to the Anvil building in Seers Village and enter the odd-looking wall and down the staircase to the workshop.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go north to the water elemental room and search the machinery to the west to get a key.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you didn't bring 2 elemental ores with you, go west and get them by killing 2 Earth elementals (Mine the Elemental Rock for them to spawn).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go south from the centre room and smelt your ores into bars, at the furnace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go down the hatch in the centre room with the key in your inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take-from the schematic crate to the south, take both schematics.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and use one bar on the workbench to make a crane claw. Note: Don't accidentally let it create more than one.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return downstairs to the two crane levers and pull the western one to lower the crane.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your claw on the old crane.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb the stairs to the south-west to get on the catwalk.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the junction box to the west.</str>
line	
line	<str>Click the pipe ends, not the pipe, to connect them as shown.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search all crates on the ground floor and the catwalk of the workshop until you find the following. IMPORTANT: Be sure to read the Crane schematic and Lever schematic, or you will be unable to find all the pieces.</str>
line	
line	<str>On the north side of the catwalk use the Pipe on the broken piping.</str>
line	
line	<str>On the east side of the Ground floor use the cogs on the pins on the side of the machine that looks like a wind tunnel as shown.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the old lever to the right.</str>
line	
line	<str>On the south side place an elemental bar on the jig cart. (under the elemental claw)</str>
line	
line	<str>First, use the western lever (by the schematics crate) to raise the crane.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the eastern lever to rotate the crane.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the western lever twice to lower the crane into the lava and back up again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the eastern lever to rotate the crane over the cart.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the western lever twice to lower the bar onto the cart and release it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever just north of the claw controls to move the cart.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the western-most lever - in front of the press station - to flatten the bar once the cart has stopped.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the yellow sign lever again to move the cart to the next station.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the northern-most lever.</str>
line	
line	<str>Turn the corkscrew lever twice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the northern-most lever again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Turn the west water valve twice so that the valve opens and closes. The tank will fill.</str>
line	
line	<str>Turn the east water valve twice so that the valve opens and closes. The tank will empty.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the northern-most lever.</str>
line	
line	<str>Turn the corkscrew lever twice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the northern-most lever to close the door.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Pull the yellow sign lever again.</col>
